text:
sara: quick RFC follow-up — we need a concrete plan for v2 -> v3 compatibility shims. want opinions on placement (runtime vs gateway) and rollout strategy.

tom: +1. my gut: do as much as possible at the gateway/proxy layer to avoid touching the low-latency runtime hot path.

akash: want to flag that some v2 behavior relies on sequence-length padding and a different response envelope. runtime-only shims might be more correct for KV cache continuity.

lia: can we split responsibilities? gateway for surface-level request/response mapping, tiny runtime adapter for KV/cache shape translation when needed. keeps perf-sensitive code minimal.

mike: agree with lia. also we should expose an opt-in header so customers can test: `X-Redwood-Compat: v2` — avoids global toggles.

sara: good. propose a hybrid: gateway does header-based routing + schema mapping; runtime has a lightweight compatibility flag to adjust KV caching keys and batch coalescing. that minimizes overhead for v3-only traffic.

akash: rough cost tradeoff: gateway mapping is CPU + network serialization, cheapish. runtime shim affects memory layout + cache hit rate — could increase latency on long seqs. need benchmarks.

lia: action: I'll prototype a middleware that rewrites v2 response envelopes into v3 shape and vice versa. sample mapping:

```js
// gateway shim pseudocode
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  if (req.headers['x-redwood-compat'] === 'v2') {
    // rewrite request body to old schema
    req.body = mapV2Request(req.body);
    res.on('finish', () => {
      // rewrite response back to v2 envelope
      res.body = mapV3ResponseToV2(res.body);
    });
  }
  next();
});
```

mike: for routing, we should support: header opt-in, per-account toggle in console, and canary percent. will need a rollout API.

sara: agree. telemetry needs: compatibility_flag, translation_latency_ms, cache_hit_ratio_delta. add these to the console dashboard.

akash: tests: unit mapping tests + e2e with recorded prompts from customer corpora. also fuzz a bunch of malformed v2 payloads.

lia: one more concern — function-calling / tool outputs changed shape in v3. runtime shim must avoid silently dropping tool-calls. propose explicit failure mode: if request uses v2 header and runtime can't translate toolcall -> return 412 with a clear migration message.

tom: +1 on hard failure for unsupported cases. we can add an automatic migration suggestion that includes the minimal transform.

deploy-bot: canary deploy scheduled for gateway-shim at 2026-04-08T15:00Z (pipeline #3821).

sara: timeline proposal: 1) prototype gateway shim & unit tests (lia) — 2 weeks, 2) runtime minimal adapter + bench (akash) — 3 weeks, 3) canary rollout (mike & infra) — 1 week, 4) open beta + docs, telemetry (tom) — 2 weeks, 5) deprecation notice at 9 months, removal at 12 months.

mike: we should prepare docs and migration checklist now. I'll draft migration guide and a small compatibility test harness customers can run locally.

akash: who owns the compatibility matrix? we need a doc listing every endpoint/field that changed and recommended shim.

sara: owner: tom will maintain the matrix. lia will PR the gateway shim prototype into `compat/gateway-proxy`. akash will bench runtime impact and add feature flag. mike handles rollout automation and console toggles.

lia: volunteer for early code review for the gateway shim.

tom: I'll create the compatibility matrix doc and link it from the RFC. putting owners in the RFC follow-up thread.

sara: thanks — please add any blockers here. we should aim to have an initial canary in two weeks to capture early edge cases.

mike: minor blocker: infra quota for canary GPUs if we need runtime benching at scale. I'll request extra capacity.

akash: noted. also add perf target: <5% median latency increase for v3 traffic when runtime adapter toggled off. if exceeded, we fallback to gateway-only translation.

sara: final: add a deprecation header in responses for v2-mode: `X-Deprecation-ETA: 2027-04-01` and a link to migration guide. keeps customers informed.

deploy-bot: note: staging tests 82/84 passed for `compat/gateway-proxy` branch.

sara: cool — thanks everyone. I'll consolidate action items and update the RFC follow-up doc.
